Z||000000||Howard_Sacks||12-21-2001||08:20 PM||||My 86GT has been sitting for over a year waiting for me to figure out what to do with it.  Well, today I finally put the front hubs and brakes and other misc  stuff on and tonight it's off jackstands.  A big thanks to forum members and other fiero people I met over the internet for helping me out.  Specifically: Jon, Keith, Pat, Chris, Brian, West Coast Fiero (Chris and Eric for answering ALL of my fiero questions even if not related to products that I bought) and Rodney(for those hard to find parts)<P>The Car at 11:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.howard.saturnet.net/fiero/rollercoaster/onstands2.jpg"> <P>The Car now:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.howard.saturnet.net/fiero/rollercoaster/offstands2.jpg"> <P>The car isn't running yet but we should be by new years.||||reg||10
Z||000001||GTFiero1||12-21-2001||09:10 PM||||hey w your in cherry hill! if youever want to sell a fastback anytime soon, lemme know im looking for one under $1,500. i want one as my first car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Adam J. B.<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero_3.jpg">   <BR>you gotta keep on keepin on...<BR>IM AOL: GTFiero &  Rumpdetective (dont ask)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Howard_Sacks||12-22-2001||12:49 PM||||Adam, I'm not interested in selling. I've put WAY more than $1500 into this car: engine, shocks, struts, springs, mounts bushings. . .I'm not going to add it up :-O<P>You can find a fastback for ~$1500, but it's definitely going to need work.  I got my 87GT for $1060/w tax, but it needed close to $1k and 6 months to get it "right" and on the road.  And that's without labor because I did all the work but the alignment myself.<P>Unless you want a project, I would budget $2500 and buy one that doesn't need work.<P>Also, make sure you take it for a spin in the wet in a vacant parking lot before you go on the road.  I found out after my first left in the wet (managed to hit a curb and bend a control arm) that fieros handle slighty different than 4wd jeeps(or whatever car you're practicing on).||||reg||1
